# Angular component file layout

Every Angular component uses three sibling files:

```
feature-name.component.ts
feature-name.component.html
feature-name.component.scss
```

## Rules

- Do **not** use inline `template:` or `styles:` in `@Component`.
- Use `templateUrl` and `styleUrl` pointing to sibling files.
- Keep TypeScript files for logic only: class, imports, lifecycle, methods.
- Put all markup in `.html` and all component-scoped styles in `.scss`.

## Example

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-example',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [FormsModule],
  templateUrl: './example.component.html',
  styleUrl: './example.component.scss'
})
export class ExampleComponent {}
```

When adding a new component, create all three files together. When editing an existing inline component, split it before making other changes.
